# 027 - int of a non-Str is a TYPE error, not the identity on Int (§6/.41 D).
# Same reasoning as 022: unary_type_mismatch is the only §4-legal constructor
# error.rs offers for a one-operand type complaint.
--- source
print int(5);
--- expect
error: Type at line 1: int expects a Str operand, got Int
